# Audit test fixtures.
#
# These plugins have to be real files on disk. `boltdocs audit` reads a plugin's
# package directory statically — package.json, the entry it declares, the install
# script it declares — and skips a directory that is not there. A fixture that is
# not committed is a fixture that silently audits *nothing*.
#
# The parent `packages/core/.gitignore` ignores `node_modules/`, which is right
# for every real dependency and wrong here: these four packages are test inputs,
# not dependencies. Negating the rules below re-includes them, and the audit
# tests were failing on this, not on the code they test.
#
# `packages/core/tests/audit/fixtures/project/.gitignore` also ignores the marker
# files the audit must never create — those stay ignored, because a marker on
# disk is a test failure and not a fixture.

!/
!node_modules/

# Everything under the fixture's node_modules is checked in *except* the
# markers. The marker patterns live in the file above, so the two rules
# compose: the negation keeps real packages, the marker rules keep the
# "proof the audit did not run the plugin" files out.
!node_modules/evil-plugin/
!node_modules/evil-plugin/**
!node_modules/clean-plugin/
!node_modules/clean-plugin/**
!node_modules/sneaky-plugin/
!node_modules/sneaky-plugin/**
